# Subagents

**Before non-trivial work** (multi-file edits, research, implement, review — not a typo or one-liner):

1. **Read** `pack-shared/subagents.md`

Default: hand the job to a **Task** with a Worker Brief so the main chat stays lean (decide, ask the user, integrate, gates). Sequential Tasks are fine when there is only one job. When lanes are independent, launch **parallel** Tasks in the same turn.

Trivial work (typo, pure rename, git status, reading existing terminals) may stay on the main agent. Never spawn verification-only MCP/lint ritual Tasks.

Worker Brief **Read first** must include `taste/doctrine.md` and `architecture/doctrine.md`.

When this plugin is installed, prefer these named agents for the matching job: **explorer** (research), **architect** (structure), **implementer** (write slice), **reviewer** (local diff), **pr-reviewer** (open GitHub PR). Do not use reviewer for a GitHub PR, and do not use pr-reviewer for a local branch.
